From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 20:53:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Onefile: take the payload's compression level from the
 environment

The payload is compressed at level 22, whose window is so large that
zstd compresses a payload of any likely size as one job: with sixteen
workers, a 156 MB payload took 102 seconds against 105 on one. At level
19 the workers share it, 19 seconds, for a payload 1.3% larger.

NUITKA_ONEFILE_COMPRESSION_LEVEL, when set, is the level, clamped to
1..22. The compression cache already keys each file on the level.
---
 nuitka/tools/onefile_compressor/OnefileCompressor.py | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/nuitka/tools/onefile_compressor/OnefileCompressor.py b/nuitka/tools/onefile_compressor/OnefileCompressor.py
index ba60678..3cbf1be 100644
--- a/nuitka/tools/onefile_compressor/OnefileCompressor.py
+++ b/nuitka/tools/onefile_compressor/OnefileCompressor.py
@@ -31,7 +31,15 @@ from nuitka.Version import version_string
 
 
 def getCompressorLevel(low_memory):
-    return 3 if low_memory else 22
+    if low_memory:
+        return 3
+
+    level = os.environ.get("NUITKA_ONEFILE_COMPRESSION_LEVEL")
+
+    if level:
+        return max(1, min(22, int(level)))
+
+    return 22
 
 
 def getCompressorFunction(expect_compression, low_memory, job_limit):
